<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Peaceful</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>change peaceful
</pre>
<p>Switches you between peaceful and aggressive mode.
</p><p>When you are <b>aggressive</b>, you strike back at once when someone 
offends you: when someone attacks you, casts a harmful spell at you, or 
is caught trying to steal from you, you start fighting them, if you are 
awake. "They will come in peace and leave in pieces."
</p><p>When you are <b>peaceful</b>, you mostly don't, and can decide for 
yourself whether to fight: "You will no longer attack aggressors." You 
don't strike back at spells cast on you, nor at anyone you catch trying 
to steal from you or to bash you.
</p><p>New characters start out peaceful, unless they are evil. Peaceful mode 
is handy when a friend casts a spell on you that counts as harmful, such 
as summon: you won't turn on them for it.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
